{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.FreeAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.RingQuot","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":39,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.central_tail_collapses_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.central_tail_collapses_all","kind":"theorem","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L495-L509","doc":"**The answer to `qou-p8yg`'s open question: no tail assignment exists.**\n\nIf any generator of the tower maps to a central element, every generator below it\nmaps to that *same* element. In a finite target the `far` relations make the high\ngenerators central, so the entire image collapses to one element and `g 0` cannot\nbe separated from `g 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.central_forces_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.central_forces_below","kind":"theorem","line":475,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L475-L493","doc":"**A central generator collapses the whole tower below it**, by induction on\nthe distance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.central_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.central_step","kind":"theorem","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L464-L473","doc":"One step of the collapse: a central generator drags the generator below it\nonto itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.braid_central_forces_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.braid_central_forces_eq","kind":"theorem","line":445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L445-L462","doc":"**Braiding with a central element forces equality.** If `y` is central, both\n`x` and `y` satisfy the Hecke quadratic, and the two braid, then `x = y`.\n\nBoth sides of the braid relation collapse onto `h • (y * x)` plus one leftover\nterm — `x` on the left, `y` on the right — so the relation *is* `x = y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.tail_scalar_is_automatically_a_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.tail_scalar_is_automatically_a_unit","kind":"theorem","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L398-L419","doc":"**The unit hypothesis above is free, so the exclusion is total.**\n\n`scalar_tail_forces_central` assumes the tail scalar is a unit, and the one\napparent escape from it would be to send the tail to a *non*-unit scalar. There\nis no such escape: the tail generator `g m` is itself sent to `c·1` and must\nsatisfy the **same** Hecke quadratic, which forces `c·(c − h) = 1` outright —\nso `c` is a unit automatically, whenever `algebraMap` is injective (true for the\nrank-6 candidate, which is an algebra over a field).\n\nConsequently every tail-to-scalars assignment is excluded, not merely the\ninvertible ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.scalar_tail_forces_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.scalar_tail_forces_central","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L365-L396","doc":"**The tail-to-scalars route is dead.** If the scalar `c` is a unit, the\nadjacent generator `x` is forced to be *central* — so it commutes with every\nother generator's image, and no such map can separate `g 1` from the subalgebra\ngenerated by `g 0` in any algebra where those two fail to commute.\n\nApplied to the rank-6 candidate: `σ₁` would have to commute with `σ₀`, which it\ndoes not. Hence strict growth needs the Iwahori-Hecke coset basis, or the direct\nlimit of `SchurWeyl.HeckeInclusion.heckeIncl` together with injectivity — not a\nfinite separator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.braid_scalar_forces_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.braid_scalar_forces_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L341-L363","doc":"**A generator adjacent to a central scalar satisfies a scalar relation.**\nIf `y = c·1` and `(x, y)` satisfies the braid relation while `x` satisfies the\nHecke quadratic, then `c·(c − h)·x = c·1`. No hypothesis on `c` is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.tower_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.tower_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L309-L316","doc":"**The missing quadrant, in one statement.** For *every* `h` — in particular\nevery `h ≠ 0`, unlike the symmetric-group tower where the generators are\ninvolutions and `h = 0` is forced — there is a tower whose generators satisfy\n`σ² = h·σ + 1` **and** whose filtration is non-constant, unlike\n`unitMarkovTrace`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.heckeTower_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.heckeTower_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L300-L307","doc":"The tower is non-trivial: `0 ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twH_zero_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twH_zero_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L284-L298","doc":"**The filtration is not constant.** `H 0 ⊊ H 1`, so this witness is not the\ndegenerate `H = ⊤` tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twH_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twH_zero","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L278-L282","doc":"The bottom of the filtration is the scalars. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.algebraMap_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.algebraMap_gen","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L276-L276","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.heckeTowerMarkovTrace_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.heckeTowerMarkovTrace_H","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L268-L269","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.heckeTowerMarkovTrace_g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.heckeTowerMarkovTrace_g","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L265-L266","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.heckeTowerMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.heckeTowerMarkovTrace","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L235-L263","doc":"**A `MarkovTrace` on the presented infinite Hecke tower**, for any `h` and any\nroot `z` of the Hecke quadratic. With `h = q - q⁻¹` the root is `z = q`.\n\nThe filtration is the tower's own `Algebra.adjoin` filtration and `h` is free, so\nthis inhabits the quadrant no previous witness reached: non-constant filtration\n(`twH_zero_lt_one`) **and** `h ≠ 0` available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.towerTrace_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.towerTrace_apply","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L232-L233","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.towerTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.towerTrace","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L227-L230","doc":"The tower trace: collapse to `H₂`, then take the rank-2 Ocneanu trace.\n🛑 Not faithful — see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.ocneanuTrace_markovInv_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.ocneanuTrace_markovInv_gen","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L218-L223","doc":"**(T3') for a general element**, with `zinv = z - h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.ocneanuTrace_markov_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.ocneanuTrace_markov_gen","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L210-L216","doc":"**(T3) for a general element.** Stabilisation holds for all of `H₂` iff `z`\nis a root of `X² - h·X - 1` — the same quadratic as `ocneanuTrace_mul_defect`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.collapse_twGenInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.collapse_twGenInv","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L197-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.collapse_twGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.collapse_twGen","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L193-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.collapse","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L181-L191","doc":"Every generator of the tower is sent to the single generator of `H₂`. This is\nan algebra map precisely because `Hecke2` satisfies all three relations: `quad`\nis `sigma_sq`, and `braid` / `far` are trivial for a single element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twH_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twH_mono","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L174-L177","doc":"The filtration is increasing. **This is `≤`, not strict** — see the module\ndocstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGenInv_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGenInv_mem","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L170-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen_mem","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L167-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.mul_twGenInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.mul_twGenInv","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L163-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGenInv_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGenInv_mul","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L159-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen_far","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L151-L155","doc":"**Distant generators commute** in the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen_braid","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L144-L149","doc":"**The braid relation** in the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen_quad","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L138-L142","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic relation** in the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twH","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L132-L134","doc":"The tower's own filtration: `H n` is generated by the first `n` generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGenInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGenInv","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L129-L130","doc":"The inverse generator `σ_m⁻¹ = σ_m - h·1`, forced by the quadratic relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.twGen","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L125-L127","doc":"The Hecke generator `σ_m` in the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeTower","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L122-L123","doc":"**The infinite Hecke tower** `H_∞`, presented by generators and relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeRel.far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeRel.far","kind":"ctor","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L118-L120","doc":"Distant generators commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeRel.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeRel.braid","kind":"ctor","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L114-L117","doc":"The braid relation on adjacent generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeRel.quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeRel.quad","kind":"ctor","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L112-L113","doc":"The Hecke quadratic relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.HeckeRel","kind":"inductive","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L109-L120","doc":"**The defining relations of the infinite Iwahori-Hecke tower.** With\n`h = q - q⁻¹`, these are exactly the relations of `H_n(q)` for every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.fgen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness.fgen","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeTowerWitness.lean#L106-L107","doc":"The `m`-th free generator of the free `R`-algebra on `ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}